      "evidence": "The Statement defines the coefficient polynomials on “E:=D(ρ/4)” and says they have coefficients in holomorphic functions on E (lines 53–57), but clauses 2–3 require identities “on D_j” (lines 62–66). For j=1, Q₁=2; the cited domain rule D_k=D(ρ/2−2bk), with b=ρ/(8Q₁), gives D₁=D(3ρ/8), strictly larger than E. For x∈U, Z=x+i(5ρ/16)e₁ lies in D₁\\E, so P₁ is not defined there as stated. The clauses need to restrict the identities to E or explicitly define the extensions to D_j.",
